    <decisions>
        <description>Checks the Opportunity&apos;s record type to decide which Beacon Feedback surveys to create: Sales Demo and Sales Prospecting for Subscription New, Onboarding Call 1 - Kick Off and Customer Call for Subscription Renewal.</description>
        <name>Opportunity_Record_Type</name>
        <label>Opportunity Record Type</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Other Record Type</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Subscription_New</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.RecordType.DeveloperName</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Subscription_New</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Sales_Demo_Record_Type</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Subscription New</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>Subscription_Renewal</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.RecordType.DeveloperName</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Subscription_Renewal</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Onboarding_Call_1_Record_Type</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Subscription Renewal</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Checks that the Beacon Feedback Customer Call record type (Customer_Call) was found. If it was, builds the Customer Call survey. If not, skips it and goes straight to Create Beacon Feedback Records, so a missing record type never creates a survey with a blank record type.</description>
        <name>Was_Customer_Call_Record_Type_Found</name>
        <label>Was Customer Call Record Type Found?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Create_Beacon_Feedback_Records</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Not Found</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Customer_Call_Found</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Customer_Call_Record_Type.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Assign_Customer_Call_Feedback</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Customer Call Found</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Checks that the Beacon Feedback Onboarding Call 1 - Kick Off record type (Onboarding_Call_1_Kick_Off) was found. If it was, builds the Onboarding Call 1 - Kick Off survey. If not, skips it and moves on to Get Customer Call Record Type, so a missing record type never creates a survey with a blank record type.</description>
        <name>Was_Onboarding_Call_1_Record_Type_Found</name>
        <label>Was Onboarding Call 1 - Kick Off Record Type Found?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
